{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 3.761, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 5396}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5396, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6931, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 431, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_017DVJb7iQYQeFACFiQ3VXu2", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "The hh channel fits well \"so long as h is produced close to rest\" (non-relativistic Higgs). Best fit (Tab. fitResults): m_χ ≈ 125.7 (+3.1/−0) GeV, ⟨σv⟩ ≈ 5.33 (±0.68) ×10^-26 cm³/s, χ²_min = 29.5, p-value = 0.13. That mass is about 2.6 times the b b̄ best fit of 48.7 GeV. The paper's explanation is that hh can be treated as a cascade annihilation: each h decays mainly to b b̄, and each b has energy m_h/2. The b quarks are therefore boosted/less energetic than in direct χχ→b b̄ (where E_b = m_χ), so a good fit is obtained even though m_χ is more than twice as large as for the other channels.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1411.4647v2", "section_id": "4.1"}, {"arxiv_id": "1411.4647v2", "section_id": "4.4"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261117T082844Z_eval-14_staged_286f", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The hh channel fits well \"so long as h is produced close to rest\" (non-relativistic Higgs). Best fit (Tab. fitResults): m_χ ≈ 125.7 (+3.1/−0) GeV, ⟨σv⟩ ≈ 5.33 (±0.68) ×10^-26 cm³/s, χ²_min = 29.5, p-value = 0.13. That mass is about 2.6 times the b b̄ best fit of 48.7 GeV. The paper's explanation is that hh can be treated as a cascade annihilation: each h decays mainly to b b̄, and each b has energy m_h/2. The b quarks are therefore boosted/less energetic than in direct χχ→b b̄ (where E_b = m_χ), so a good fit is obtained even though m_χ is more than twice as large as for the other channels.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1411.4647v2", "section_id": "4.1"}, {"arxiv_id": "1411.4647v2", "section_id": "4.4"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 9.241, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 21567, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 830, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 12327, "cache_read_input_tokens": 12238, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-17T08:28:53+00:00"}
